---
import Docs from '../layouts/Docs.astro';
const repo = 'https://github.com/abhiudayg/shipnote';
const code = 'mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-white/[0.08] bg-black/60 p-5 font-mono text-[13px] leading-7 text-zinc-300';
---

<Docs title="Setup: shipnote" description="Fork shipnote, set one variable, and run the nightly commit dataset on your own GitHub account." active="/setup/">
  <p class="font-mono text-xs tracking-wider text-sky-400 uppercase">Setup</p>
  <h1 class="text-gradient mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.035em] md:text-5xl">Run the nightly dataset</h1>
  <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-7 text-zinc-400">You need a fork, two settings, and one manual run. The nightly job then runs on your own account.</p>

  <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">1. Fork the repository</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-zinc-400">Fork <a href={repo} class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">abhiudayg/shipnote</a> on GitHub.</p>

  <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">2. Enable Actions</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-zinc-400">Forks have GitHub Actions turned off. Open the Actions tab in your fork and enable workflows.</p>

  <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">3. Set DATASET_AUTHOR</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-zinc-400">Add a repository variable named <code class="font-mono text-zinc-200">DATASET_AUTHOR</code> under Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → Variables. Use the git author name or email on your commits. Check them with:</p>
  <pre class={code}><code>git config user.name
git config user.email</code></pre>

  <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">4. Build the first dataset</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-zinc-400">Open Actions → shipnote nightly dataset → Run workflow, and set <code class="font-mono text-zinc-200">days</code> to <code class="font-mono text-zinc-200">30</code>. Scheduled runs use 30 days by default.</p>

  <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Schedule</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-zinc-400">The workflow runs at 18:30 UTC, which is 00:00 IST. To change the time, edit the cron expression in <code class="font-mono text-zinc-200">.github/workflows/nightly-dataset.yml</code>. GitHub can start scheduled runs several minutes late, and public repositories disable scheduled workflows after 60 days without activity.</p>

  <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Run it locally</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-zinc-400">Requires <code class="font-mono text-zinc-200">git</code> and the GitHub CLI, signed in with <code class="font-mono text-zinc-200">gh auth login</code>.</p>
  <pre class={code}><code>LOGIN=your-github-login AUTHOR="Your Name" DAYS=7 scripts/export-commits.sh out</code></pre>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-500">LOGIN and AUTHOR are required. DAYS defaults to 30. Output goes to out/&lt;owner&gt;/&lt;repo&gt;.patch.</p>
</Docs>
